9 thefollowingnewparagraph:
10 V. School boards and the board of trustees of chartered public schools shall develop and
11 adopt a policy governing the use of student cell phones and other personal electronic communication
12 devices in schools. Such policy shall prohibit all personal communication device use by students
13 from when the first bell rings to start instructional time until the dismissal bell rings to end the
14 academic school day, with approved exceptions determined by the superintendent or their designee
15 with respect to student medical, disability, or language proficiency need or specific educational
16 purpose. Such policy shall be developed in collaboration with school parents and teachers and shall
17 bereviewedannually. Schooldistrictandcharteredpublicschoolpoliciesshallnotprohibitstudents
18 withmedical needs, suchas insulinpumps and glucosesensors, or disabilities from usingadeviceto
19 support their learning as identified by their individualized education program (IEP), plan developed
20 under Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, 29 U.S.C. section 794, or when required to
21 support emergent multilingual students with appropriate language access programs and services
22 pursuanttoTitleVIoftheCivilRightsActof1964.
23 2 EffectiveDate. ThisactshalltakeeffectJuly1,2025.
